# PERF-RADIX-2 MSD bucketing — 2026-06-10 ("try radix" chunk 2, unblocked
# by empiricism)
#
# THE PROOF THAT UNBLOCKED THIS (load-bearing finding): equal-key-run
# representative choice is byte-IRRELEVANT. Probe: merge walk flipped to
# pick the LAST index of each equal run (a maximally different
# representative) — hash-locks 36/36 AND terminal/clic097/noaa e7
# lossless bytes identical. The packed dedup key covers every
# downstream-read field, so ANY sort producing lexicographic key order
# with arbitrary equal-run internal order is byte-safe. This dissolves
# the radix-chunk-1 theoretical blocker.
#
# Change: dedup sort for n >= 16384 is now MSD counting-sort by the
# 16-bit BE key prefix into 65536 buckets (one count pass + one
# scatter), then per-bucket pdqsort with the full-key comparator,
# parallel across buckets (disjoint &mut ranges). Concatenation is full
# lexicographic order; small n keeps the plain index sort.
#
# Gates: bytes identical 5/5 A/B cells (DIFFERENT algorithm, same
# bytes — the proof in action); hash-locks 36/36 x2; lib 1488; it 81.
#
# A/B (8 iters/side, loadavg 4.2-6.5 — moderate-busy):
#   noaa -2.39%  city12mp -1.64%  terminal -0.68%  clic097 -0.40%
#   clic028 +1.47%
# Lean-positive 4/5; magnitudes within the busy-box envelope — treat as
# indicative until a quiet grid; structurally superior (smaller sorts,
# bucket-parallel, no rayon merge passes).
# Host: lilith (7950X, WSL2).
